{"availability":"available","full":"AVGVSTVS96/hex","name":"hex","description":"A personal assistant that lives in your Telegram, built on Claude Code.","category":"Developer tools","language":"CSS","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-04T22:13:39Z","updated":"2026-10-10T10:29:37Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hex-sand.vercel.app","topics":[],"demo":"https://hex-sand.vercel.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:47.234Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:47.234Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T11:06:47.234Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T11:06:47.234Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["built in 6 hours at the Personal Agents Hackathon because I wasn't happy with all the other options, this is my version of the personal assistant - as simple, elegant, portable, and modifiable as humanly possible - more capable than any other assistant on the market (Dots, Instinct, Grok Bot, Hermes, OpenClaw) - clean and solid foundation to build on, claude code updates immediately benefit hex with no modification - relies on an auto-maintained fork of Anthropic's telegram + discord connectors which support multiple threads per channel collectively, we still have a lot of work to do before…","Claude Code as your personal assistant. It runs on your own machine, and you talk to it in Telegram, Discord and Buzz. hex-sand.vercel.app","hex runs wherever Claude Code does, on a machine that stays on (a home server, a Mac that doesn't sleep, a cloud VM), with your own Claude subscription, and Opus 5.5 does the thinking. It's a handful of plain files around Claude Code: no framework, no database, no service manager required. One small hub process holds the bot connections and starts a Claude Code session for each conversation."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AVGVSTVS96/hex/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"050e54c899fa77d293f706eadedf48b63b3f595f9df263584bcc